---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Refund Policy"
  description="Thirty days, no questions asked, on a first OraDiscuss membership. Renewal charges are refundable within thirty days of the charge."
  updated="August 2026"
>
  <p>
    <strong>Our promise: thirty days, no questions asked.</strong> We would rather return your
    money than hold a membership you regret. You do not have to justify the request, and asking for
    one is not held against you.
  </p>

  <h2>Your first membership purchase</h2>
  <p>
    A full refund within <strong>30 days</strong> of your first membership purchase, no questions
    asked. It does not matter how much you downloaded or read in that time. That is the point of the
    window: it exists so you can actually use the thing before deciding.
  </p>

  <h2>Renewal charges</h2>
  <p>
    A renewal charge is refundable within <strong>30 days of that charge</strong>. If a renewal
    caught you by surprise, that window is there for exactly this reason.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can also stop a renewal before it happens. Cancelling through the customer portal link on
    your Paddle receipt ends future billing while leaving the year you already paid for intact.
  </p>

  <h2>What happens when a refund is issued</h2>
  <p>
    Access ends when the refund is issued. Downloads you already have on your machine are yours to
    keep and remain under the licence in the <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a>, but member
    downloads, new pack versions, the Security Watch briefs and the Academy stop with the
    membership.
  </p>

  <h2>How to request one</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:support@oradiscuss.com">support@oradiscuss.com</a> from the address you
    bought with, or use the customer portal link on your Paddle receipt. Because Paddle is our
    Merchant of Record, an approved refund is processed by Paddle back to your original payment
    method, typically within a few business days.
  </p>

  <h2>The one abuse rule</h2>
  <p>
    Refunding and rejoining repeatedly to reset a launch price forfeits that locked launch price. It
    is the only condition attached to any of the above, and it exists so that the lifetime price
    lock stays honest for the members who simply stay.
  </p>

  <h2>Your legal rights</h2>
  <p>
    This policy is in addition to any mandatory refund or withdrawal right you have under your local
    consumer law, for example in the EU or the UK. Nothing here removes those rights.
  </p>
  <p>This Refund Policy forms part of our <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
